(version 1)

# Board clearance follows Mantis: 0.1 mm (Default and Power classes), hole to hole 0.2 mm, copper to edge 0.2 mm.
# The RF class stays at 0.2 mm: that gap to the ground pour sets the 50 ohm coplanar line, so it is load-bearing.
#
# BGA855N6 LNAs (U3, U4) are TSNP-6-10: 0.4 mm pitch with 0.25 mm pads leaves 0.15 mm between pads, so the RF pins
# and their fan-out sit 0.15-0.2 mm apart inside the part. Both footprints carry a 0.15 mm local clearance for
# pad-to-pad; this rule gives the tracks and vias inside each courtyard the same allowance against the RF class's
# 0.2 mm. Zone fills keep their own clearance. Values need their unit: a bare number here silently disables the rule.
(rule "TSNP-6-10 LNA pin fan-out"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.Type != 'Zone' && B.Type != 'Zone' && ((A.intersectsCourtyard('U3') && B.intersectsCourtyard('U3')) || (A.intersectsCourtyard('U4') && B.intersectsCourtyard('U4')))"))
